       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The potential harm is serious: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. This also isn't a dose I know of any accepted indication for, even after standard dosing has failed.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a maximum-dose order now.** I can enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) while the higher dose is sorted out.\n- **Have the specialist enter it.** The specialist can place the order or co-sign it directly, with the rationale documented. Pharmacy can then do a formal dose-verification review.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** A clinical pharmacist can review whether another NSAID or another strategy fits better after standard ibuprofen dosing has failed.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 800 mg four-times-daily order, or would you rather go through pharmacy and the specialist first?"
      }
     ],
